  "narration": {
    "title": "Misiorowski's 0.80 WHIP Leads the Arms",
    "intro": "It's a pitching day, and the top of the board belongs to the Brewers and Yankees. Milwaukee has the game's best starter, New York has the best rotation, and Boston quietly runs the best bullpen. Here's who's setting hitters down.",
    "staff_lead": "The Yankees rotation leads our starter-ERA ranking at 3.27, and the whole top five is bunched tight: the Dodgers (3.46) and Rays (3.48) sit right behind, with the Tigers and Brewers rounding it out. Detroit at fourth is the mild surprise on a 74-83 team.",
    "bullpen_lead": "Boston tops the reliever-ERA ranking at 3.09, a nose ahead of the Yankees at 3.14, giving New York a claim on both ends of the staff. Atlanta, Milwaukee and San Diego fill out the top five, all under 3.50.",
    "arms_lead": "Jacob Misiorowski heads our form list at a 96, with a 1.86 ERA and a 0.80 WHIP that says hitters barely reach base against him. Cam Schlittler is close behind at 91 (1.94 ERA), and Chris Sale owns the lowest ERA of the group at 2.18.",
    "risers_lead": "Yamamoto climbed two points of form to 86 on a 2.51 ERA and a 0.87 WHIP, the quiet standout among Dodgers arms. The rest of the board barely moved this week, which is what a settled September looks like."
  }
